---
import LegalLayout from "../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "October 11, 2026";
const effectiveDate = "October 11, 2026";

const sections = [
  { id: "about", title: "1. About these terms" },
  { id: "free-and-pro", title: "2. Free and Pro" },
  { id: "subscriptions", title: "3. Subscriptions" },
  { id: "accuracy", title: "4. Accuracy" },
  { id: "not-medical", title: "5. Not medical advice" },
  { id: "contact", title: "6. Contact" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Wayfoot Terms of Use"
  description="The terms that apply to the Wayfoot step counter and its Pro subscription."
  lastUpdated={lastUpdated}
  effectiveDate={effectiveDate}
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="about">1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms apply to <strong>Wayfoot</strong>, the step counter published by
    NexUtility. They add to the general
    <a href="/terms">NexUtility Terms of Service</a>, which also apply. Where
    the two differ, this page applies to Wayfoot.
  </p>

  <h2 id="free-and-pro">2. Free and Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Counting steps, the daily goal, the widgets and the watch apps are free.
    The free version shows the last 7 days of history. <strong>Wayfoot Pro</strong>
    shows your full history and lets you export it as a CSV file.
  </p>

  <h2 id="subscriptions">3. Subscriptions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Wayfoot Pro is sold as an auto-renewing subscription. The price and period are shown before you buy.</li>
    <li>Payment is charged to your Apple or Google account when you confirm the purchase.</li>
    <li>The subscription renews automatically unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the end of the current period.</li>
    <li>
      You can manage or cancel it at any time in your App Store or Google Play
      account settings. Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription.
    </li>
    <li>Refunds are handled by Apple or Google under their own policies.</li>
    <li>If you reinstall the app or use another device with the same store account, use Restore purchases to get Pro back.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="accuracy">4. Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    Wayfoot shows the steps and distance that your phone, watch or tracker
    recorded. It does not measure them itself, and those figures are
    estimates. When no measured distance exists, Wayfoot estimates distance
    from your step count.
  </p>

  <h2 id="not-medical">5. Not medical advice</h2>
  <p>
    Wayfoot is a general activity tool. It is not a medical device and does
    not diagnose, treat or prevent any condition. Talk to a doctor before
    changing your activity if you have a health concern.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">6. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:hello@nexutility.dev">hello@nexutility.dev</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
